WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.990
It is Friday afternoon.

2
00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:06.460
In many Jewish homes, everything
is being made ready before sunset.

3
00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:10.420
In Orthodox homes, the cooking
must be finished in time.

4
00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.460
Then candles are lit.

5
00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.620
In Orthodox homes, until
nightfall on Saturday,

6
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:19.740
no one will switch on a
light, drive or use a phone.

7
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:25.560
So why would someone choose not to switch
on a light for 25 hours every week?

8
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:29.460
In this mission, you'll read what
the Torah says about the seventh day,

9
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.060
and follow Shabbat at home
from candles to Havdalah.

10
00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.930
Then you'll see how Jews
keep the day differently,

11
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.310
and how prayer shapes every ordinary day.

12
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.380
Your mission: explain why someone would
choose not to switch on a light for 25

13
00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.790
hours every week.
